Version 0.84
   *Faster handling of received packets. Received data now 
    reaches the TNC about twice as fast, so acks, digipeats and PBBS 
    replies go out sooner, especially after long frames. In testing, acks 
    after 128-byte frames came about 0.75 seconds sooner.

   *Less wasted work when idle. The TNC no longer gets “transmit buffer 
   empty” interrupts while it isn’t transmitting.

   *No settings change, and saved settings and PBBS messages carry over 
   when you update.
